  "core": "Breakthrough shatters what no longer holds — a wall that blocked becomes rubble that clears. Seated in its own position, the breaking turns back on breaking itself: even the method of shattering can be shattered when it hardens into routine. In proportion, only what has genuinely stopped working gives way. The opening stays open, and the capacity to break through remains alive for what truly needs to change.",
  "sheetLine": "Even the old way of breaking can be broken when it becomes the next wall."
